hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer a question from one of  my youtube viewers a mirror who wrote it  asking about business plans so he wrote  saying hi Evan I absolutely love your  videos when creating the business plan  and I'm writing that does it have to be  with all the confusing terms or can it  be in plain English so thanks for the  question Amir first of all of your  business plan you never wanted to be  confusing you don't want to be confusing  for you you aren't be confusing for any  of the readers so as much as you can put  it in plain English plain language so  that everybody can understand it  depending what your plan is the for the  business plan is it's something that  you're just going to use internally to  help you build your business or if  you're also going to use it to go and  get investors or that you get a bank  loan it's gonna be read by other people  then you really have to make sure it's  in plain English because they're not  going to know your business as well as  you do so quick example when I was in  the venture capital business I got so  many business plans people wanting to  get funding and a lot of it was not in  plain English it was a very technical a  lot of people with great new  technologies and I'm sure to them when  they read over their business plan it  made a lot of sense like this is what we  do but for somebody who is looking at it  doesn't know your business it's a lot of  technical jargon so you want to make  sure that you can you can really put it  in simple terms easy to understand that  anybody can understand a lot of these  bankers investors they may be  knowledgeable but you're in the stream  but they're not going to know it as well  as you will know it so it's really  important to put it in terms that  everybody can understand so for those  ones usually they got rejected sometimes  if we saw something we might you know  bring them in but for the most part it's  the ones who had the really clear no  simple to understand business plans that  we call them to be able to meet them  because we understood what they do and  they clearly explained their value  proposition so hopefully that helps one  last thing when we look that business  plans there's a term within the venture  capital industry called the grandmother  test and it basically means is your  business plan written so that your  grandmother can understand it and you  know great task  once you finish your business plan show  it to your grandmother show it to your  friends and family people kind of know  what you do but they don't know the  specifics and not technical people show  it to them and if they can understand  what the opportunity is and how you  solve a problem and are able to really  help people but they can get that from  your business plan then you're ready to  start giving it to investors and bankers  if they read it and they have still no  idea what you do then it's time to go  back to the drawing board and recreate  it especially that executive summary  that first part the executive summary is  really important that's the first thing  that somebody's going to read if they  can't understand the exec summary then  forget it you're gone usually look at  the exec summary then we look at the  management team and see who's behind it  and then we look at the financials and  if all that made sense then we start  reading the rest of the business plan so  really make sure that your executive  summary is especially written in plain  English so that helps them here if you  guys like the video for you who are  watching please give it a thumbs up  below it helps you know which readers  you like and which ones you don't like  as much but I was like making these  videos and appreciate seeing those  thumbs up come in and if you have a  thought about business plans you want to  add something to this video to help a  mere or you have another question for me  feel free to leave 